{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lg4ew7dz","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 2 Offline","year":2007,"examDate":2007,"subject":"physics","chapter":"heat-and-thermodynamics","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"kinetic-theory-of-gases-and-gas-laws","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pstatement-1p-pthe-total-translational-kinetic-energy-jee-advanced-physics-motion-95whc2cimlp1kwq1","content":"<p>STATEMENT 1</p>\n<p>The total translational kinetic energy of all the molecules of a given mass of an ideal gas is 1.5 times the product of its pressure and its volume.</p>\n<p>Because</p>\n<p>STATEMENT 2</p>\n<p>The molecules of a gas collide with each other and the velocities of the molecules change due to the collision.</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement-1 is True, Statement-2 is True; Statement-2 is a correct explanation for Statement-1."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement-1 is True, Statement-2 is True; Statement-2 is NOT a correct for Statement-1."},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement-1 is True, Statement-2 is False."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement-1 is False, Statement-2 is True."}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>Statement 1 :</p>\n<p>Total translational kinetic energy <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.84ex\" height=\"2.736ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.2 3907.3 1209.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(1055.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1849.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2449.3,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"52\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-52\"></use><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\" transform=\"translate(736,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>where,</p>\n<p>n = no. of moles</p>\n<p>R = gas constant</p>\n<p>T = Temperature</p>\n<p>but, PV = nRT</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> K.E. = 1.5 PV</p>\n<p>Statement 2 : Molecules of a gas collide with each other and the velocities of the molecules change due to collision.</p>\n<p>But statement 2 is not a correct explanation of statement 1 .</p>"}]}